# Always commit and push completed Helseapp web work

After finishing a feature or fix for the Vercel web app (`public/`, `api/`, `lib/`), **automatically commit and push to `origin`** without waiting to be asked.

## When to commit and push

- Do this once the work is complete and ready (not mid-experiment).
- Skip if Frøydis explicitly says not to commit/push for that change.
- Skip if there is nothing relevant to commit.
- Skip (and warn) if the only changes are secrets or high-risk files (e.g. `.env`, credentials).

## Git safety (always)

- Never force push.
- Never amend unless all standard amend conditions are met.
- Never skip hooks (`--no-verify`, etc.).
- Never update git config.
- Never commit secrets (`.env`, credentials.json, and similar).

## What to include

- Only stage files related to the completed work.
- Leave unrelated Expo / server / Terra / Pace / local noise uncommitted unless it was part of the task.
- Prefer clear, why-focused commit messages (1–2 sentences).

## After push

Briefly tell Frøydis:

1. The commit hash (short SHA is fine).
2. That Vercel will deploy from `origin`.
